-- title:
--   Coefficient sets and residual points for predictions
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let earlier candidates $i\in I$ have parents $\mathrm{par}(i)\in P$ and points $y_i$, and let $b$ be a base point.
--
--   1. **Grouped coefficients.** $\theta^p_i=\theta_i$ if $\mathrm{par}(i)=p$ and $0$ otherwise, with group mass $\sum_i\theta^p_i$.
--   2. **Coefficient set.** Nonnegative $\theta\in\mathbb R^I$ with every group mass at most $1$. It is a compact subset of the coefficient box.
--   3. **Residual point.**
--   $$
--   r_p(\theta)=b+\sum_i\theta^p_i\,(y_i-b),
--   $$
--   a convex combination in which the base point receives the unassigned mass of group $p$. Two residual points differ by at most $\sum_i|\theta_i-\theta'_i|$ times the diameter.
